{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 30, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJapan. The word itself conjures images of ancient temples, bustling cities, and serene gardens. My recent trip lived up to every expectation and then some!\n\nI started in Tokyo, a sensory overload in the best way. Neon lights, delicious street food (ramen, takoyaki – I tried it all!), and the organized chaos of Shibuya Crossing were unforgettable. I explored the vibrant Harajuku district, indulging in quirky fashion and colorful treats.\n\nNext, I took the Shinkansen (bullet train!) to Kyoto. The contrast was striking. Here, history whispered from every corner. I wandered through Fushimi Inari Shrine with its thousands of vibrant red torii gates, and found peace in the Arashiyama Bamboo Grove.  A traditional tea ceremony was a highlight – a truly calming and respectful experience.\n\nBeyond the iconic sights, it was the small moments that truly resonated. The impeccable politeness of the people, the artistry in every detail, and the deliciousness of even the simplest meals.  \n\nGetting lost in the backstreets of Osaka, discovering hidden ramen shops, and marveling at the craftsmanship of local artisans – these are the memories I'll cherish. Japan is a country of beautiful contradictions, a place where ancient traditions seamlessly blend with modern innovation. It’s a trip I highly recommend – prepare to be amazed!\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0012646066024899483}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.14694757759571075}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -9.536738616588991e-07}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0020534161012619734}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.11282681673765182}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.11384062469005585}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -0.16682201623916626}, {"token": "Japan", "logprob": -0.57635